# ============================================================================
# minotaur — FIRST-DRAFT .blob generated from the reference mesh's vertex
# clouds. Every number is measured; its line's `# fit:` comment names the
# source. len=/dir= come from the RIG chain — joint-to-joint x one scale —
# because a bone's head is its parent's TAIL and overlapping vertex clouds
# do not compose into a chain (the first draft stood ~0.3 m off the floor
# on summed cloud extents). The cloud owns the SURFACE: bands split at
# radial-profile inflections, radii are band medians, and offset= carries a
# surface that sits off its bone (rig joints sit 9-13 cm from the skin —
# offset the PRIMS, never relocate the bone). Angles exist only where
# dirVector is invertible.
#
# NOT attempted — not derivable from a Meshy reference; add by hand:
#   fingers (the rig lumps each hand into one joint), bend= on any bone,
#   angles on side/fwd bones, mottle colour, jaw/nose/brow shaping.
#
# Budget: 72/80 prims (68 authored + 4 face),
# worst cluster legR at 15/40. The shader's hard ceilings are
# 128 prims total — which derived wound bones SHARE — and 64 per cluster,
# where the fold SILENTLY stops; half of each is left for refinement.
# TRIMMED 52 least-evidenced band(s) to stay inside. Re-run the draft after
# refining so any cut you undo is re-measured, not silently restored.
#
# Chain: grounded — the root shifted 0.0526 m so the built body's
# lowest surface sits at y = 0; built extent 1.217 m against the
# 1.2168 m height line (+0.02%).
#
# Hand pass owed:
#   pelvis: cloud residual 0.1345 m RMS about its axis — wants a bend=
#   chest: cloud residual 0.0905 m RMS about its axis — wants a bend=
#   spine2: cloud residual 0.0448 m RMS about its axis — wants a bend=
#   skull: cloud residual 0.0914 m RMS about its axis — wants a bend=
#   clavicle: cloud residual 0.1041 m RMS about its axis — wants a bend=
#   upperarm: cloud residual 0.0759 m RMS about its axis — wants a bend=
#   forearm: cloud residual 0.0591 m RMS about its axis — wants a bend=
#   hand: cloud residual 0.0492 m RMS about its axis — wants a bend=
#   thigh: cloud residual 0.1097 m RMS about its axis — wants a bend=
#   shin: cloud residual 0.0793 m RMS about its axis — wants a bend=
#   foot: cloud residual 0.0921 m RMS about its axis — wants a bend=
#   pelvis band 1: rotated cross-section — the axes cannot say it
#   pelvis band 2: rotated cross-section — the axes cannot say it
#   pelvis band 2: paint splits mid-band — colour boundary owed
#   pelvis band 7: rotated cross-section — the axes cannot say it
#   pelvis band 7: paint splits mid-band — colour boundary owed
#   pelvis band 8: paint splits mid-band — colour boundary owed
#   pelvis band 10: rotated cross-section — the axes cannot say it
#   chest band 1: rotated cross-section — the axes cannot say it
#   chest band 1: paint splits mid-band — colour boundary owed
#   chest band 9: rotated cross-section — the axes cannot say it
#   chest band 9: paint splits mid-band — colour boundary owed
#   skull band 1: paint splits mid-band — colour boundary owed
#   skull band 4: rotated cross-section — the axes cannot say it
#   skull band 4: paint splits mid-band — colour boundary owed
#   skull band 5: rotated cross-section — the axes cannot say it
#   skull band 5: paint splits mid-band — colour boundary owed
#   clavicle band 1: rotated cross-section — the axes cannot say it
#   clavicle band 10: rotated cross-section — the axes cannot say it
#   clavicle band 10: paint splits mid-band — colour boundary owed
#   clavicle band 15: rotated cross-section — the axes cannot say it
#   upperarm band 1: rotated cross-section — the axes cannot say it
#   upperarm band 1: paint splits mid-band — colour boundary owed
#   upperarm band 7: rotated cross-section — the axes cannot say it
#   upperarm band 7: paint splits mid-band — colour boundary owed
#   forearm band 1: rotated cross-section — the axes cannot say it
